ow checks as `code`. A green PR Integration job proves its tree, so an up-to-date PR's squash merge skips the bigdisk jobs on `main`. A repository adopts v1.41 in one CI-file PR and sizes its PR runner capacity for integration on every PR. v1.40 (2026-11-16, owner ruling 732): a library behind a newer upstream release never fails CI. The deps-check step passes `DEPS_CHECK_LAG=report` on every event, so the shared [depscheck](../deps/depscheck/README.md) v1.1.0 reports every lag and fails only a vulnerable go.mod requirement, a lookup failure, and a fork replace or pseudo-version with no reason comment on a line the change adds or bumps; the daily `deps-bump.yml` v1.1.0 keeps the full gate and carries every lag as one PR. A repository adopts v1.40 in one CI-file PR with `scripts/depscheck` v1.1.0, the Makefile's `$(if $(DEPS_CHECK_LAG),-lag $(DEPS_CHECK_LAG))` argument and `deps-bump.yml` v1.1.0. v1.39 (2026-11-14, ruling 640, owner decision 222 (a)): `make deps-check` fails a library behind its latest release only when the change adds that go.mod requirement or changes its version, or when govulncheck reports a version of a go.mod requirement vulnerable (a stdlib, toolchain or indirect-only finding is reported, not failed); a lag the change did not touch is reported, not failed. A new lint-job step, `Base commit for deps-check (ruling 640)`, fetches one commit at depth 1 (a pull request's base sha, the merge ref's first parent, or a push's `before`) and passes it as `DEPS_CHECK_BASE`; a schedule or `workflow_dispatch` run has none and keeps the full gate. The preflight refusal of a `workflow_dispatch` off main exempts `ci/deps-bump`, which runs the PR tier, because `deps-bump.yml` dispatches CI there. A repository adopts v1.39 in one CI-file PR with the shared [depscheck](../deps/depscheck/README.md) at `scripts/depscheck`, its Makefile's `deps-check` and `deps-bump` targets, and `deps-bump.yml`. v1.38 (2026-11-14, owner ruling 633, decision 219(d); go-xkms #1384): 