f-hosted pools supply GOCACHE, GOMODCACHE, CI_HOST_CACHE, Athens GOPROXY and the dev-cache Trivy mirrors. v1.35.3 (2026-11-12, Tenant Agent m2586): `pull_request` also fires on `ready_for_review`, so a draft marked ready gets its CI run. v1.35.2 (2026-11-11, Tenant Agent m2577): the `Signatures` job moves to `signatures.yml`, so CI Gate no longer needs it; adopt with `signatures.yml` and `.github/allowed_signers` in one CI-file PR. v1.35.1 (2026-11-11): the `Signatures` job fails closed when a named base cannot be read, and its signature-presence check cannot fail on a long signed message. v1.35 (2026-11-11, Tenant Agent m2557, owner ruling on commit signing): a `Signatures` job, a `pr` job in CI Gate's needs, checks every commit in the range (base..head on a pull request, before..after on a push to `main`) with `git verify-commit` (`gpg.format=ssh`, `gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile`) against `.github/allowed_signers` read from the base commit, and requires the key's registered principal to be the committer email; a commit GitHub made (committer `noreply@github.com`) passes only when the API reports it verified with committer `web-flow`. It fails closed on an unsigned commit, an unknown key, a principal mismatch or an unreadable API, printing the commit and why. A repository adopts v1.35 in one CI-file PR that also adds its `.github/allowed_signers` from [`../signing/`](../signing/README.md). v1.34.1 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2226 item 2, ruling 377): `GO_BUILD_PROXY` has no trailing `direct` (dependency-resolution.md, no direct fetch anywhere); adoption PRs carry v1.34.1. v1.34 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2211 item 2(b)): the `changes`, `schedule-guard` and `arch-gates` jobs are one `preflight` job (the guard first, nothing checked out before it), so the template has 8 jobs, not 10; CUSTOMIZE jobs read `needs.preflight.outputs.*`, and each repository merges its unit and race shards into one job in its adoption PR. v1.33.2 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2113 item 3, with InfoSec): the `Releasability (private patterns)` step does not fail on a matched line that carries the InfoSec waiver `lab-string-ok: <reason>` on the same line, with the colon and a reason; it lists each waived line as a notice, path and line only, with the count. A bare marker still fails ([public-hygiene.md](../../conventions/public-hygiene.md) "Internal values stay private", rule 5). v1.33.1 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2107 item 4): comments only; the pattern file's source is named as dept-infosec `security/internal-names.patterns`. v1.33 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2104 item 2): the releasability step accepts the five classes of the regenerated pattern file, `coord-host`, `internal-email`, `lab-address`, `lab-host` and `owner-path` (optional `/i`); the image namespace comes from the repository variable `CI_IMAGE_NAMESPACE`. v1.32 (2026-11-08, Tenant Agent m2098 item 2, InfoSec finding): the `Releasability (private patterns)` step reads each pattern line as `class<TAB>regex` (class `lab-address`, `lab-host` or `owner-path`, optional `/i`; blank and `#` lines skipped), fails on a malformed line, an unknown class or a regex `grep -E` refuses, printing the line number only, and runs `git grep -i -E` over the regex fields. v1.31 grepped each whole line with `-F`, so nothing matched and the gate was green for a false reason; no repository merges v1.31. v1.31 (2026-11-07, Tenant Agent m2069 item 3): the `Releasability (private patterns)` step in the lint job checks the tracked tree against the private pattern file from the Actions secret `RELEASABILITY_PATTERNS` (source in platform-configs) and prints path and line only; `RELEASABILITY_TEST` names no internal value ([public-hygiene.md](../../conventions/public-hygiene.md) "Internal values stay private"). **CUSTOMIZE:** set the secret on each repository. v1.30 (2026-10-31, Tenant Agent m1804): the five fixes of the 72-hour evaluation ([ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §12): the toolchain image from the registry cache (`ci-image-cache.sh`, the `publish-images` job on the release runner), a proven tree skips the main full tier, path-scoped `lint-gates` and no `lane-ckpt/*` PRs, a timeout on every job, `make gosec` in the PR tier and no dispatch off `main`. Needs `make gosec` and `make docker-build-toolchain`. v1.29.5 (2026-10-30, ruling 262(a)): one change, the `GO_BUILD_PROXY` separator is `|` (`<DEVCACHE_GOPROXY>|https://proxy.golang.org|direct`), as everywhere else ([devops.md](../../conventions/devops.md) §2a), because Go falls through a `,` only on a 404 or 410 and through a `|` on any error. The repository's Makefile quotes the value on its docker build line (`--build-arg "GO_BUILD_PROXY=$(GO_BUILD_PROXY)"`, [devcontainer.md](../../conventions/devcontainer.md) §4), where an unquoted `|` is a shell pipe. A repository adopts v1.29.5 in the one CI-file PR that adopts v1.29.4, with that Makefile line. v1.29.4 (2026-10-30, ruling 261(c), claude-agents #379 comment 157032): each `make docker-build` passes `GO_BUILD_PROXY=<DEVCACHE_GOPROXY>,https://proxy.golang.org,direct` (v1.29.5: `|`) when the runner sets `DEVCACHE_GOPROXY` and Athens answers a 5-second probe, so the image and Lint Gates builds fetch through Athens with the public fallback ([devops.md](../../conventions/devops.md) §2a); the schedule guard reads `waiting` before `in_progress`, so no run starting between its two queries goes uncounted (trusted-firmware's fix); and it requires `in-toolchain-image.sh` v4. A repository adopts it in one CI-file PR that takes both files and keeps its CUSTOMIZE blocks. v1.29.3 (2026-10-29, ruling 255(10)/(11)(c)): one schedule run per repository, skipped when a `main` run is in flight. A schedule run's concurrency group is `schedule-{repository}`, and a new `schedule-guard` job skips every bigdisk job, and CI Gate with them (`skipped`, never green), while the workflow has a push run on `main` in progress or waiting; it fails closed when the API gives no count ([ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §10 (h)). A bigdisk CUSTOMIZE job adds `schedule-guard` to its needs and the guard clause to its `if:`. A repository adopts it in one CI-file PR, which can ride its v1.29.2 adoption bump PR. v1.29.2 (2026-10-28, ruling 239(8)): comments only. A `CUSTOMIZE` job that runs only when certain paths change needs `[changes, image]`, and its `if:` tests an output that the image job's build step sets (such as `needs.image.outputs.built == 'true'`) together with the changes output. On a pull_request, an `if:` that read only `needs.changes.result == 'success'` or only `needs.changes.outputs.<path> != ''` left the job skipped unstarted in two runs; the form that tests the image job's output started it. No repository adopts it by PR. v1.29.1 (2026-10-27, ruling 226(15), 108 repair): lint fails fast. The `lint-gates` job runs `make lint-gates` without `-k`, so the first failing gate ends the step; under `-k`, go-quicbaas run 68949's Lint took 51.5 min, 37 of them after its `go vet` failure. Every other job, gate and tier is v1.29.0's. v1.29.0 (2026-10-27, ruling 220(5) and 221(4), handbook #474; [ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §9): the Alpine package index checksum joins the integration image's tag hash. A new "Read the Alpine package index" step runs `apk-index-sum.sh` into `APK_INDEX_SUM` in each job that names the integration image (image, lint-gates, integration, soak), so none waits for the image job; the repository's `make -s it-image` hashes it and `make docker-build` passes it as a build argument ([devcontainer.md](../../conventions/devcontainer.md) §6), so a new Alpine package release, a CVE fix among them, changes the tag and forces a rebuild (go-enclave main fd83b79ce, CVE-2026-92392). Every job, gate and tier is v1.28's. A repository adopts v1.29 in one PR with `apk-index-sum.sh`, its Makefile's `APK_INDEX_SUM` and its Dockerfile `integration` stage's `ARG APK_INDEX_SUM` and `apk upgrade --no-cache`. The parallel stage jobs (ruling 220(7)) move to v1.30: `runs-on` cannot take a needs output on Gitea 1.27.1 (run 68501), and the registry-push question is with the owner (169). v1.28.0 (2026-10-26, ruling 219(3); [ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §8): `make deps-check` joins the PR tier as a lint-class gate. Its image-job step drops the `CI_FULL_TIER` condition and runs on every event, a docs-only PR included, as `make lint` does, with `IN_IMAGE_NETWORK=bridge` for the module proxy; it stays on the full tier. A module behind its dependency floor now fails the PR rather than `main` after the merge (go-objstore main 8946d5f53, fixed by go-objstore #127). The image job is already `pr` in CI Gate, so the gate's needs and results lines do not change. Each repository adopts v1.28 as a CI-file PR, and none hand-patches its `ci.yml` ahead of the template. v1.27.0 (2026-10-25, Tenant Agent m1192 (6), item 27, dept-software #710; [ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §10 (g)): a new `lint-gates` job runs the repository's `make -k lint-gates` in the toolchain image in parallel with the image job's `make lint`, not in series after it. It runs only when the Makefile or a tracked `*.mk` defines a `lint-gates` target, and otherwise prints OK and passes without building an image. It builds the images as the image job does (`make docker-build`, then `make -s toolchain-image`), skips on a draft, and is a `pr` job in CI Gate's needs and results check. `make lint` and `go vet` do not change. A repository whose `make lint` lists `lint-gates` removes it from the lint target, and one that ran `make lint-gates` as a lint or image job step drops the step, in the PR that adopts v1.27. `IN_IMAGE_NETWORK` on its step (`CUSTOMIZE`, default `none`) gives the gates a network. v1.26.2 (2026-10-24, Tenant Agent m1167 (5), ruling 145): one change, the concurrency group. `main` is keyed per event and sha (`main-{event}-{sha}`), so a merge never cancels the `main` run in progress; go-luks2, go-enclave, go-qrdb, go-objstore, trusted-firmware and xkey-android already run this form, and go-xkms #1692 and go-trusted-platform #1022, which key `main` by `github.sha` alone, are also per sha. A PR ref is one group and `cancel-in-progress` stays a literal `true`. v1.26.1 (2026-10-24, Tenant Agent m1128 (9), handbook #429 P1 2): a docs-only PR runs the repository's releasability test, `RELEASABILITY_TEST` (CUSTOMIZE), after `make lint`; `make coverage` runs it on every other PR. v1.26 (2026-10-24, Tenant Agent m804 item 3, m809 item 3; ruling 137; [ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §10 (f)): a draft pull request runs no CI; every job skips on `github.event.pull_request.draft` and CI Gate fails on a draft. Marking the PR ready starts no run, and there is no `edited` or `ready_for_review` trigger: the PR's own lane pushes an empty commit when it leaves draft. v1.25.4 (2026-10-21, from xkey-android #40's Codex review): `pull_request` lists `types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]` and leaves out `labeled`. Gitea 1.27.1 reports every label add and remove as `labeled` with no label in the payload, so each `task:*` or `code-review` change started a run that cancelled the PR's run in progress (go-trusted-platform #853; go-qrdb, go-xkms and trusted-firmware already carried the line). A `ci:full` label takes effect on the PR's next push or update-branch, or through `workflow_dispatch` ([ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §8). v1.25.3 (2026-10-21, from a Codex review): the reaper's in-use check and its `docker image rm` were two calls, so a job could lease and re-tag between them and still lose the tag. The reaper's image loop, each lease step and every re-tag now take one lock per Docker daemon: a created, never-started container named `<prefix>image-lock`, made from an empty image `<prefix>image-lock:base` imported when it is missing. The daemon refuses a second container of that name. A lock created more than 600 s ago is a dead hol