e bare host name (the Tenant Agent's read of the Codex P1s on go-quicbaas #2667 and go-trusted-platform #2311; Infra creates the secret on each repository from the existing variable; `testdata/ci-mask-lan-tests.py` M1 to M5, which takes a copy's path); a job output never carries a registry address, since GitHub drops an output that contains a masked value: a job that hands an image to another exports only its tag or digest, and each consumer rebuilds the reference from the secret `CI_IMAGE_REGISTRY` after its own mask step (the Tenant Agent's read of the Codex P1 on go-trusted-platform #2311; `testdata/job-output-handoff-tests.py` H1 to H5, which takes a copy's path); main's concurrency group is `main-{event}` again, so a newer push to main cancels the older main run; v1.26.2's per-sha group (ruling 145) let superseded main runs queue ahead of PR work. **Rollout: a ci.yml-only PR per repository, separate from code-review.yml and not waiting for it, trusted-firmware and go-qrdb first**, carrying v1.52's runner selection so internal pull requests run on our runners. v1.52 (2026-11-21, Tenant Agent order, defect fix): a fork's pull request under `pull_request` reached a self-hosted runner, since `preflight`'s runs-on had no fork check and the runner selection could overflow the run to the Dells. A pull request whose head repository is not this repository now runs every job on `ubuntu-latest`: `preflight`'s runs-on adds a fork clause before `CI_PREFLIGHT_RUNS_ON`, and `Hosted or overflow runner (ruling 1024)` outputs the hosted default for a fork's head with no API call. `Runner labels (ruling 633)` gives a fork's head under `pull_request` no unset-variable exemption, as under `pull_request_target`. Same-repository pull requests, pushes and Gitea are unchanged. Tests: `testdata/runner-labels-tests.py` part H, `testdata/runner-select-tests.py` part E. Adopt as a one-file bump. v1.51 (2026-11-21, ruling 633 hardening): `Runner labels (ruling 633)` also reads every runs-on