n `[self-hosted, linux, x64, release]`, and pull request jobs never do. `publish-images` takes that label; on GitHub it runs only when the repository variable `RELEASE_RUNNER` is `true`, on Gitea as before. The preflight step `Runner labels (ruling 633)` fails CI when a job that names `release` could run for a pull request (a), or its `if:` does not restrict it to a push to `refs/heads/main` or `refs/tags/`, or a `workflow_dispatch` on main (b); tests in `testdata/runner-labels-tests.py`. The `bigdisk-docker` pools get a rootless Docker daemon of their own at the same `/var/run/docker.sock`, so workflows need no change, but images and containers do not persist between jobs, `--network host` is the rootless namespace's network, and `-v $GITHUB_WORKSPACE:...` still mounts an empty path. A repository adopts v1.38 in one CI-file PR that also moves its release.yml jobs from `ubuntu-latest` to the release label, pins its build and scan images by `@sha256` digest and pulls them by digest before `docker create` or `docker run`, and sets `RELEASE_RUNNER` only after Infrastructure reports the release pools live ([ci-standard.md](../../conventions/ci-standard.md) §3a). v1.37 (2026-11-13, ruling 580): every job in every template carries `timeout-minutes` so a hung job ends itself; ceilings by kind are 60 for unit, race, lint and other test jobs, 120 for integration, image builds, soak and release, 10 for gates and aggregators; a repository sizes each job at or under its ceiling from 1.5 x its longest green run, and a job whose green runs need more keeps its measured value. v1.36 (2026-11-13, owner approval: keep CI caches local): a self-hosted job never touches the Actions cache; every `actions/setup-go` step takes `cache: ${{ runner.environment != 'self-hosted' }}`, and an `actions/cache` step runs only when a `$CI_HOST_CACHE` lookup missed. The self-hosted pools supply GOCACHE, GOMODCACHE, CI_HOST_CACHE, Athens GOPROXY and the dev-cache Trivy mirrors. v1.35.3 (2026-11-12, Ten